    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 56 tests pass, including the new `Cp45Tests`. **BUILD SUCCESS.**\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `salutation` feature: an optional request `title` (MR/MRS/MS/DR) that produces `salutation` = `title + ' ' + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given.\n\nBecause the acceptance flow round-trips through `POST /api/owners` \u2192 persist \u2192 `GET /api/owners/{id}`, the `title` had to be stored so it survives to the GET response. Changes:\n\n1. **Owner entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a persisted `title` column with getter/setter.\n2. **DB schemas** \u2014 added a `title` column to the `owners` table in all four schemas (hsqldb is the test profile with `ddl-auto=none`, so this was required; h2/mysql/postgres added for parity).\n3. **openapi.yml** \u2014 added `title` to the `OwnerFields` input schema (documenting MR/MRS/MS/DR) and a read-only `salutation` to the `Owner` output schema.\n4. **OwnerMapper** \u2014 added a `salutation(owner)` derivation and mapped it into `OwnerDto`. The input `title` maps into the entity automatically (String\u2192String by name).\n\nThe mapper follows the existing computed-field pattern (`displayName`, `initials`, etc.), and `title` is optional so all existing tests are unaffected.",
